<code>assert Objects.checkIndex(index, \old(this.size())) => \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.get(index).equals(oldValue);</code>

However, since we need to refer to the value before the removal, we should use `\old` to capture the state before the method execution. Here's the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert this.get(index).equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>

But since `get(index)` after the removal will throw an `IndexOutOfBoundsException`, we should directly compare with the `oldValue` which captures the element at the index before removal:

<code>assert oldValue.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>

So the final assert statement is:

<code>assert oldValue.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert Objects.checkIndex(index, \old(this.size())) => \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
